         && callsignsMatch(parsedMessage.destination, m_myCallsign)
         && callsignsMatch(parsedMessage.transmitter, decode.callsign);
 
+    // RRR/RR73/73 addressed to us belong to an exchange already in progress.
+    // If native queue ownership disappears near the end of a QSO, admitting
+    // one as a fresh target restarts at the signal-report stage (for example,
+    // replying R-11 to RR73).  MSHV still receives the decode and can finish
+    // its active QSO; AutoDX must never create a new target from it.
+    if (target.isCallingMe && parsedMessage.isExchangeOnly) {
+        target.isCallingMe = false;
+        target.priorityReason = "Exchange-only reply is not a new caller";
+        return target;
+    }
